1
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and take a look from a distance,
would you?

2
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:42,740
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

3
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:47,200
Fuhahahahahahahahaha!

4
00:00:56,320 --> 00:00:59,940
Anyone without a job, come to my place.

5
00:01:00,820 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

6
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:18,260
Look, Aganeru is burning too.
It'll work out somehow, eventually.

7
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:27,480
You understand, right? Got it, got it.
Once you do, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,160
Make money with the healing type.

9
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:50,640
She's the healing type, isn't she?

10
00:01:51,740 --> 00:01:53,060
She's so soothing.

11
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:55,280
She's so soothing.

12
00:01:56,240 --> 00:01:57,580
Welcome!

13
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:00,680
Which flower should I pick?

14
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:03,360
That big one over there is nice too, right?

15
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:10,120
I love those! Right, we've got some
cosmos that came in this morning.

16
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,780
Right? She's so cute, isn't she?

17
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:18,560
Really, she's incredibly cute.

18
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,180
Every single day.

19
00:02:22,860 --> 00:02:27,520
Bringing home flowers you can't even eat,
and it's so healing

20
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:34,300
Healing, right? Healing, healing...
wait, were you guys that hurt to begin with?

21
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:37,800
We're getting hurt every single day!

22
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:40,540
What's hurting you so much?

23
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:44,920
Well, human relationships,
work pressure, and all sorts of things.

24
00:02:45,840 --> 00:02:48,480
We're not strong like Ryotsu.

25
00:02:48,860 --> 00:02:50,780
We may look strong at first glance,

26
00:02:50,780 --> 00:02:53,980
but really,
we're as delicate and fragile as glasswork,

27
00:02:53,980 --> 00:02:56,800
we're people who get hurt easily.

28
00:02:56,800 --> 00:02:58,000
Glasswork?

29
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:01,800
Where on that muscle-flaunting
body are you fragile or delicate?

30
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:04,000
Delicate is right here.

31
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,920
That's exactly it, senpai.

32
00:03:08,020 --> 00:03:11,341
Ryo-chan, you should try learning from
Honda and the others once in a while,

33
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:13,280
and buy a flower or two, why don't you?

34
00:03:13,780 --> 00:03:16,340
These guys don't care about flowers at all.

35
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:18,902
Healing type or whatever, I don't know,

36
00:03:18,952 --> 00:03:22,300
they just want to see the
face of part-timer Hana-chan.

37
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,480
Senpai.

38
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:25,700
Welcome back, Kei-chan.

39
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:29,720
Speaking of Hana-chan,
I hear she has a college boyfriend.

40
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,540
Volvo-san and the others were here?

41
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:40,360
I just happened to overhear the
flower shop manager talking over there.

42
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:41,500
I don't know.

43
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:42,180
Flowers.

44
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,900
Because I didn't want to
hear about her boyfriend.

45
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,800
What should we do, senior?

46
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:51,840
Don't worry, I'll take Hana-chan's place.

47
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,620
From now on, I'll heal you guys.

48
00:03:54,620 --> 00:03:55,620
How?

49
00:03:55,620 --> 00:04:00,580
Even if I don't look it, I've been called
the healing-type officer of Kameari.

50
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:01,640
Nyan nyan.

51
00:04:02,460 --> 00:04:04,160
I've never heard of that.

52
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:05,900
Hey, cheer up.

53
00:04:05,900 --> 00:04:08,420
Stop it, that's going to haunt my dreams.

54
00:04:09,040 --> 00:04:10,300
I'll heal you.

55
00:04:11,560 --> 00:04:13,840
Please stop hurting us any more than this.

56
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,680
I was trying to lighten
the mood for you guys.

57
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:20,240
When you're the senior,
we've never once felt relaxed, you know.

58
00:04:20,780 --> 00:04:21,140
What?

59
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:25,260
Most of our stress

60
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:27,840
can be blamed entirely on Ryotsu,
and that's no exaggeration.

61
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:29,860
That's an exaggeration.

62
00:04:31,160 --> 00:04:32,280
You trampled all over us.

63
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:33,800
Ryo-chan.

64
00:04:33,800 --> 00:04:34,780
Shut up.

65
00:04:34,780 --> 00:04:36,380
I said, shut up.

66
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,340
Reiko-san.

67
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:40,160
Why are you taking Ryo-chan's side?

68
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:41,720
I didn't do anything.

69
00:04:45,540 --> 00:04:47,980
Sorry I'm late.

70
00:04:47,980 --> 00:04:52,160
I've got a souvenir, look.

71
00:04:52,940 --> 00:04:54,900
What's with the persimmons?

72
00:04:55,420 --> 00:04:57,760
Old Mrs. Yoshida from Block Three,

73
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,720
she gave them to me because her tree had so many,
so I should take some.

74
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:03,380
Sakonji-kun and the others are here too.

75
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,300
It's still hard!

76
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:11,920
These are astringent persimmons,
aren't they?

77
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:14,660
I thought so.

78
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:17,540
If you thought so, say so!

79
00:05:17,960 --> 00:05:20,560
But Ryo-san, you eat them the
moment you're about to say something!

80
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:23,200
If we make these into dried persimmons,
we can eat them, right?

81
00:05:23,200 --> 00:05:24,440
I'll go wash them.

82
00:05:26,020 --> 00:05:27,420
What a carefree fool.

83
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,660
That's strange.

84
00:05:31,160 --> 00:05:33,060
Having Grandma here really lightens the mood,
doesn't it?

85
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:34,980
She's really healing, isn't she?

86
00:05:34,980 --> 00:05:37,000
Yes, very healing.

87
00:05:37,480 --> 00:05:39,600
Well then, we should be going.

88
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,980
Sorry for the disturbance.

89
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,620
Cheer up, okay?

90
00:05:44,480 --> 00:05:47,820
What's this? The crow that was crying
a moment ago is already laughing!

91
00:05:48,440 --> 00:05:50,880
We're so relieved Terai-san came back.

92
00:05:50,880 --> 00:05:52,040
Yes, really.

93
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,000
That should do it.

94
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:02,320
Whoa! You scared me!

95
00:06:02,660 --> 00:06:04,800
What is it, Ryo-san?
You want some tea or something?

96
00:06:05,420 --> 00:06:05,820
No.

97
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:08,440
You're acting weird, Ryo-san.

98
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:11,800
Are you perhaps a "healing" type?

99
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:15,900
What is this place?

100
00:06:16,740 --> 00:06:18,340
It's the Institute of Healing Studies.

101
00:06:18,640 --> 00:06:20,960
Institute of Healing Studies? What's that?

102
00:06:21,340 --> 00:06:23,600
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

103
00:06:29,580 --> 00:06:36,440
Executive Director of the All-Japan Healing Studies Society,
Dr. Iyashi Ōkura, forty years devoted solely to research, today

104
00:06:38,100 --> 00:06:41,460
I am an expert in healing research.

105
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:44,560
In order to survive this
harsh modern society,

106
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:47,280
healing types are an indispensable presence.

107
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,920
I see, I see.

108
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:59,100
These are all photos of people
with a healing constitution.

109
00:06:59,100 --> 00:07:00,740
A healing constitution?

110
00:07:00,920 --> 00:07:04,360
So Terai is also one of those healing types?

111
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:08,980
From what I can see,
they'd be around healing level 93 to 98.

112
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:12,200
Is that amazing or not amazing?

113
00:07:12,620 --> 00:07:15,340
Generally,
dolphins have a healing level of 150.

114
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:20,300
Iyasuke talent Inoguchi Haruko is
said to have a healing level of 98.

115
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:22,900
So that means she's pretty hot.

116
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:24,280
I don't understand at all.

117
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:27,440
Well then,
let's get right into the experiment.

118
00:07:35,360 --> 00:07:36,400
Please, take a look.

119
00:07:36,400 --> 00:07:39,880
The subject's data is
being sent to this monitor.

120
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:45,040
What's this red wave?

121
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:50,460
This wave represents beta waves, which are
produced when the brain is in a state of tension.

122
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:51,520
You there.

123
00:07:57,700 --> 00:07:59,940
Now a green wave has appeared!

124
00:08:00,740 --> 00:08:04,560
This is alpha waves, which are produced
when the brain is in a relaxed state.

125
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:09,840
So that student is being healed
just by looking at Terai's photo?

126
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:11,640
Yes, exactly.

127
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:12,560
You there.

128
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:17,040
Even if you tell me to say something...

129
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:20,260
Whoa, another alpha reading just went up!

130
00:08:20,260 --> 00:08:21,740
Amazing.

131
00:08:22,180 --> 00:08:22,540
You there.

132
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:31,640
These results far exceed my expectations.

133
00:08:32,260 --> 00:08:33,080
Seriously?

134
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:36,700
If you doubt it,
why not experience it for yourself?

135
00:08:37,860 --> 00:08:41,320
I see Terai every day at the police box, so

136
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,460
Now that you mention it,

137
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,120
Hey, cut it out.

138
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:48,000
They're showing up.

139
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:55,880
Really, now that I think about it, I do feel somehow healed.
Let's go home already.

140
00:08:56,300 --> 00:09:01,300
Look, look, look, it's showing this much.
I feel healed.

141
00:09:02,640 --> 00:09:04,540
I am healed.

142
00:09:07,740 --> 00:09:12,180
Terai-san's is about thirty times that of

143
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,400
healing ability has been confirmed.

144
00:09:14,400 --> 00:09:19,380
Yeah, that's why we see Terai every day.

145
00:09:19,380 --> 00:09:22,760
So that means Reiko, Nakagawa,
and I have been stress-free?

146
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:28,920
Looks like I've finally struck a gold mine!

147
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:34,500
Let's study Terai-san's
healing ability from every angle.

148
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,560
No, that's quite enough.

149
00:09:39,740 --> 00:09:41,760
Just wait a moment, Terai-san!

150
00:09:45,140 --> 00:09:46,620
I'm being called.

151
00:09:46,620 --> 00:09:49,700
Now that we know Terai has
the ability to heal people,

152
00:09:49,700 --> 00:09:53,200
we must put it to use for
making money as soon as possible.

153
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:56,020
Terai is for making money... no,

154
00:09:56,070 --> 00:09:58,340
you like helping people, right?

155
00:09:58,780 --> 00:09:59,880
Well, yes, but...

156
00:10:00,420 --> 00:10:04,740
From now on, you and I are going to heal
wounded people left and right, Terai!

157
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:07,440
What is this,

158
00:10:07,490 --> 00:10:10,240
this outfit?

159
00:10:10,240 --> 00:10:14,300
It's a standard approach,
but first we'll make a photo book of Terai.

160
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:17,640
A photo book of me?
No way, that's embarrassing!

161
00:10:17,640 --> 00:10:23,000
It's for helping people, Terai. If people can be healed by your image,
put up with the embarrassment.

162
00:10:23,580 --> 00:10:25,080
Well then, let's get started.

163
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:30,440
Yeah, that's great, Terai!
You look fantastic!

164
00:10:33,540 --> 00:10:38,320
This is Terai-guma, a healing character
that's a cross between a raccoon and Terai.

165
00:10:40,760 --> 00:10:44,360
You even made something like this. I
wonder if it really has any healing effect.

166
00:10:45,720 --> 00:10:46,480
It looks like him.

167
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,660
It's funny.

168
00:10:47,660 --> 00:10:52,380
If you give me your opinions as testers,
I'll give that one to you.

169
00:10:52,380 --> 00:10:53,160
It's cute.

170
00:10:53,160 --> 00:10:54,460
It might actually be healing.

171
00:10:54,460 --> 00:10:58,400
If the people themselves feel healed,
then the healing has succeeded.

172
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:07,300
There's a tea stalk standing up,
seven of them standing up!

173
00:11:07,300 --> 00:11:09,580
Looks like it's going to
be a good day today too.

174
00:11:10,540 --> 00:11:11,660
That's healing.

175
00:11:12,800 --> 00:11:15,000
OK, then let's start from the top, please.

176
00:11:17,220 --> 00:11:21,080
I dreamed last night that my house
loan was stretched out to 80 years.

177
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:23,600
I thought I'd drown in my night sweats.

178
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:28,560
If you get lost,
come to the Kameari Kōen-mae police box.

179
00:11:28,560 --> 00:11:30,640
Here it is, the Terai CD.

180
00:11:31,120 --> 00:11:33,800
I'll always be there for you.

181
00:11:34,460 --> 00:11:35,760
And that's all the time we have for now.

182
00:11:35,760 --> 00:11:39,340
Everyone who purchased the
healing-type officer Terai's CD,

183
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:48,380
we'll give 50 people this cute limited-edition Terai-raccoon melty goods.
If you want to be healed, hurry up.

184
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:49,880
me

185
00:12:02,860 --> 00:12:06,960
Over there is the much-talked-about healing officer,
Officer Terai.

186
00:12:06,960 --> 00:12:08,460
It's Terai-san!

187
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:10,660
The senpai is here too.

188
00:12:10,660 --> 00:12:18,360
Hello. Officer Terai's healing effect has been scientifically proven
to be ten times that of lemons and thirty times that of dolphins.

189
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,620
And you are?

190
00:12:19,620 --> 00:12:25,500
Forgive me for not introducing myself sooner.
I'm Ryotsu, Terai's manager and healing advisor.

191
00:12:25,500 --> 00:12:27,040
Healing advisor.

192
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:31,240
For anything about healing, please consult me.
Nice to meet you.

193
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,820
Saying something like that...

194
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:35,340
Will he be all right?

195
00:12:35,860 --> 00:12:37,160
Good luck, okay?

196
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:38,840
Thanks.

197
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,400
We're rooting for you.

198
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:42,280
Thank you very much.

199
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:44,900
A healing-type officer? No way.

200
00:12:44,900 --> 00:12:48,480
Every day,
I'll mentally heal you when you're hurt.

201
00:12:48,900 --> 00:12:51,640
Various healing goods are now on sale!

202
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:55,400
Kanon, are you all right?

203
00:12:56,500 --> 00:12:57,980
Please heal me.

204
00:12:57,980 --> 00:13:00,020
I'll pay as much money as you want.

205
00:13:01,060 --> 00:13:02,460
What? As much as I want?

206
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:24,880
First, as his manager and healing advisor,
I should confirm something.

207
00:13:24,880 --> 00:13:28,420
You said earlier that you'd
pay any amount of money,

208
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:30,460
right?

209
00:13:31,180 --> 00:13:34,240
Ryo-san, if I have the power to heal people,

210
00:13:34,240 --> 00:13:36,700
I want to heal as many people as I can,

211
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:40,100
but I don't want to turn it
into a tool for making money.

212
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:42,500
Listen, Terai.

213
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,580
To heal as many people as possible,

214
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:48,800
we have to sell lots of your CDs,
photo books, and plush toys.

215
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,900
That takes time, and startup capital too.

216
00:13:50,900 --> 00:13:53,800
If we spend that precious
time on just one person,

217
00:13:53,800 --> 00:13:56,920
it's only natural that we get paid for it,
isn't it?

218
00:13:57,640 --> 00:13:58,980
But I...

219
00:14:00,020 --> 00:14:01,980
I said I'd pay, didn't I?

220
00:14:01,980 --> 00:14:03,560
So you'll heal me?

221
00:14:03,560 --> 00:14:04,920
You won't?

222
00:14:04,920 --> 00:14:07,580
Terai-kun, heal him right away.

223
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:09,780
Please tell me the details.

224
00:14:09,780 --> 00:14:12,360
If there's anything I can do,
I'll gladly help.

225
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:15,860
I've tried all sorts of things up to now.

226
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:18,920
I've bought all of Mr.
Terai's healing goods.

227
00:14:19,380 --> 00:14:20,980
I did feel healed for a while, but...

228
00:14:20,980 --> 00:14:22,080
Right away, I'm back to...

229
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:23,920
Aaah...

230
00:14:23,920 --> 00:14:24,800
Still not here.

231
00:14:25,740 --> 00:14:27,320
What's not here?

232
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:30,540
The person sitting
diagonally behind Terai-san,

233
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:33,120
they still haven't even
brought their water, right?

234
00:14:34,060 --> 00:14:36,520
Even though they came
into this shop with us.

235
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:43,620
The beta waves are rising again and again.

236
00:14:44,980 --> 00:14:45,920
What the heck is that?

237
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:47,940
It's that thing, Ryo-san.

238
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:50,900
It's a custom-made
brainwave measuring device.

239
00:14:51,660 --> 00:14:54,400
Why on earth do you carry
something like that around?

240
00:14:54,920 --> 00:14:58,800
With this, you can tell at a glance
whether you're being healed or not.

241
00:15:03,780 --> 00:15:07,580
Don't tell me the meter's going to
explode if it goes all the way up.

242
00:15:07,580 --> 00:15:09,280
Hang on a second.

243
00:15:11,060 --> 00:15:12,140
Can I take your order?

244
00:15:12,140 --> 00:15:13,360
Omurice.

245
00:15:14,620 --> 00:15:18,500
One large omurice for the third seat from the back,
by the window, please.

246
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:22,340
Your omurice will be right out.

247
00:15:22,340 --> 00:15:23,840
How kind of you.

248
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:26,360
This one's good.

249
00:15:29,700 --> 00:15:30,500
Yes, thank you very much.

250
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:33,360
It's like some kind of dimensional bomb.

251
00:15:34,660 --> 00:15:37,920
Talking with Mr. Terai is so healing...

252
00:15:41,180 --> 00:15:42,300
Excuse me, move aside!

253
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:46,980
Hey, that's the taxi that man flagged down!

254
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,680
It's going up again!

255
00:15:50,700 --> 00:15:52,940
Wait! Taxi!

256
00:15:54,140 --> 00:15:55,280
P-please, go ahead!

257
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:57,300
Good.

258
00:16:01,060 --> 00:16:02,640
I've flagged down a taxi.

259
00:16:04,120 --> 00:16:04,480
Thank you very much.

260
00:16:05,600 --> 00:16:08,900
At this rate, you're going to build up so
much stress it'll be unbearable, you know.

261
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:13,780
Hey, what now?

262
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:17,360
Your eyebrows are joined together.

263
00:16:19,820 --> 00:16:21,880
Terai, hurry up and stop a taxi!

264
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:25,000
Taxi, taxi!

265
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:28,880
Where are you planning to take me?

266
00:16:28,880 --> 00:16:31,340
We're taking you home.

267
00:16:31,340 --> 00:16:34,020
If this keeps up, I'm going to lose my mind.

268
00:16:34,020 --> 00:16:37,700
Listen, until we get home, don't look
at anything, don't listen to anything.

269
00:16:37,700 --> 00:16:40,020
Just keep a calm mind.

270
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:44,640
Is this it?

271
00:16:45,720 --> 00:16:46,360
What a huge house!

272
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:49,440
Please, come in.

273
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,240
I'll make some tea for you.

274
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:57,620
There isn't a speck of dust on the floor!

275
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:06,900
It's quiet, isn't it.

276
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,420
Do you have a family?

277
00:17:09,960 --> 00:17:11,540
I live with just my father.

278
00:17:12,820 --> 00:17:13,440
Please, come in.

279
00:17:14,440 --> 00:17:18,940
Nothing here seems likely
to disturb a peaceful life.

280
00:17:18,940 --> 00:17:21,260
Well, lately I've been stuck indoors

281
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:29,020
and I just keep fluttering about,
I can't settle down.

282
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:38,900
Not even Terai's healing power works on him.

283
00:17:38,900 --> 00:17:42,020
Apparently he's so stressed that
even a fallen chopstick sets him off.

284
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:43,980
If you saw Ryo-san's room...

285
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,000
It must be some seasonal thing, I bet.

286
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,480
Just imagining it is stressful

287
00:17:59,280 --> 00:18:01,500
There, there, there, there, there.

288
00:18:02,080 --> 00:18:03,800
We can't just leave him like that,
it's too pitiful.

289
00:18:03,800 --> 00:18:06,340
Isn't there some way we can help him?

290
00:18:06,340 --> 00:18:07,320
Ryo-san

291
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:10,560
You said earlier you'd pay
any amount of money, right?

292
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,240
Yes, I'll pay, I'll pay.

293
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:15,340
Alright,
I'll build him a perfect healing palace.

294
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:17,960
But you'd better pay me
a generous reward for it.

295
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,200
Yes, please do.

296
00:18:24,140 --> 00:18:27,120
Easy, easy, easy, easy.

297
00:18:43,940 --> 00:18:45,940
It's a waterfall that
produces negative ions.

298
00:18:45,940 --> 00:18:48,280
Come over here and get healed too.

299
00:18:48,280 --> 00:18:49,680
No thanks.

300
00:18:53,080 --> 00:18:55,120
Hey! Keep supplying the water!

301
00:19:02,800 --> 00:19:04,800
You're going too far, Jo-san.

302
00:19:05,340 --> 00:19:08,020
Listen even to the babbling of the brook.

303
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:09,800
Apparently, it's healing.

304
00:19:10,380 --> 00:19:11,100
Help!

305
00:19:11,740 --> 00:19:12,140
Alright!

306
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:26,200
What now?

307
00:19:26,800 --> 00:19:29,720
It's the healing-type
endless stone embankment.

308
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:32,160
Are you being healed?

309
00:19:41,140 --> 00:19:42,620
Still not working?

310
00:19:42,620 --> 00:19:45,280
Alright, this is the ultimate weapon!

311
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:57,280
Okay, let's get started.

312
00:19:57,280 --> 00:19:59,140
Me

313
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,160
Me

314
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,200
Me

315
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:15,760
Aaaaaaah!

316
00:20:18,540 --> 00:20:21,440
If Terai's healing power is
30 times that of a dolphin,

317
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:24,740
then we'll go up against
31 dolphins plus a whale!

318
00:20:29,820 --> 00:20:30,880
That's healing!

319
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:49,860
Aaaaaah

320
00:21:01,960 --> 00:21:05,680
Mass-produced Teruo-kun... it's addictive

321
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:09,700
Teruo-kun is...

322
00:21:15,280 --> 00:21:17,840
What on earth was I doing all this time?

323
00:21:23,380 --> 00:21:25,260
How many years has it been
since I felt like this?

324
00:21:25,760 --> 00:21:26,840
It feels so good.

325
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:35,460
Teruo! Teruo!

326
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:42,400
Healing doctor, Father!

327
00:21:42,760 --> 00:21:44,440
Teruo!

328
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:45,560
Father!

329
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:50,440
Father and son?

330
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:53,080
Teruo, you're safe! Teruo!

331
00:21:53,160 --> 00:21:56,300
Father, because of me,
the house has come to this...

332
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,000
It's fine, as long as you're safe...

333
00:22:00,040 --> 00:22:02,820
I never expected you to be the doctor's son.

334
00:22:03,260 --> 00:22:05,840
It's all because I immersed
myself too much in my research.

335
00:22:05,840 --> 00:22:07,040
The family fell apart.

336
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:10,000
And my son fell into a
healing deflation spiral.

337
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,180
What's that supposed to mean?

338
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,160
The more he heals,

339
00:22:16,160 --> 00:22:18,820
the more sensitive he becomes to
the stress that falls upon him,

340
00:22:18,820 --> 00:22:20,400
and without healing, he can no longer

341
00:22:20,400 --> 00:22:23,020
even live for a moment.
It's a vicious cycle.

342
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:25,660
Also known as the healing bicycle startup.

343
00:22:25,660 --> 00:22:55,640
Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing!
Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing! Healing!

344
00:22:58,560 --> 00:22:59,780
Not at all.

345
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:07,340
The fortune I inherited from my
parents went to my research funding

346
00:23:07,340 --> 00:23:11,200
and my ex-wife's alimony and my son's tuition.
It's all gone.

347
00:23:11,980 --> 00:23:14,160
The land was also used as
collateral for my debts,

348
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:16,360
so this house is all that's left.

349
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:18,780
Don't say that so casually!

350
00:23:20,080 --> 00:23:21,580
And one more thing.

351
00:23:21,580 --> 00:23:24,160
The equipment we used for
Terai's healing power experiments

352
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:27,020
has been found to be malfunctioning,

353
00:23:27,020 --> 00:23:30,280
so all the experimental
data is considered invalid.

354
00:23:30,600 --> 00:23:31,560
W-what?!

355
00:23:32,240 --> 00:23:32,920
Camera sen!

356
00:23:33,100 --> 00:23:33,540
Camera sen!

357
00:23:34,520 --> 00:23:35,000
Kamera-sen!

358
00:23:35,040 --> 00:23:35,600
Kamera-sen!

359
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:35,960
Kamera-sen!

360
00:23:35,960 --> 00:23:36,340
Kamera-sen!

361
00:23:36,460 --> 00:23:36,780
Kamera-sen!

362
00:23:36,940 --> 00:23:37,160
Kamera-sen!

363
00:23:37,500 --> 00:23:37,580
Kamera-sen!

364
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:37,880
Kamera-sen!

365
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:37,920
Kamera-sen!

366
00:23:37,960 --> 00:23:38,440
Kamera-sen!

367
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:38,920
Kamera-sen!

368
00:23:39,020 --> 00:23:39,560
Kamera-sen!

369
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:39,960
Kamera-sen!

370
00:23:40,080 --> 00:23:40,680
Kamera-sen!

371
00:23:40,920 --> 00:23:41,240
Kamera-sen!

372
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:42,700
Kamera-sen!

373
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:45,360
Kamera-sen!

374
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:47,960
Kamera-sen!

375
00:23:49,240 --> 00:23:55,640
Kamera-sen!

376
00:23:58,060 --> 00:24:01,300
I hate beauty salons now!

377
00:24:14,780 --> 00:24:17,960
It sounds like someone is calling

378
00:24:18,540 --> 00:24:20,480
an afternoon after the rain

379
00:24:21,740 --> 00:24:24,520
I walked while looking back

380
00:24:27,460 --> 00:24:30,160
the feeling I had back then

381
00:24:31,620 --> 00:24:33,620
a strange feeling

382
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:39,500
So I walked on the
tiles of the arcade street

383
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:45,300
stepping only on the black ones

384
00:24:47,760 --> 00:24:53,560
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

385
00:24:54,480 --> 00:24:57,580
Politicians with their self-important faces

386
00:24:57,580 --> 00:25:00,920
and aunties with blue eyeshadow too

387
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:06,500
Try turning at that corner

388
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:11,720
You can meet everyone, everyone

389
00:25:12,240 --> 00:25:19,660
There's a wall over there,
well, surely there's a wall

390
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:24,880
Everybody come on over, come to our town!

391
00:25:31,920 --> 00:25:33,740
What's with this weird old guy?

392
00:25:33,740 --> 00:25:35,720
Goshogawara or wherever he's from,
I don't care.

393
00:25:35,720 --> 00:25:38,020
Dragging his whole gang of
underlings along behind him.

394
00:25:38,020 --> 00:25:40,020
Everybody's annoyed, right?

395
00:25:40,020 --> 00:25:42,980
And why does he have to recite
a haiku every single time?

396
00:25:42,980 --> 00:25:46,960
Next time, you pesky old man
from Goshogawara, you're on.

397
00:25:48,700 --> 00:25:50,520
That's Kameari over there.

398
00:25:51,940 --> 00:25:53,880
Well, surely Kameari.

399
00:25:53,880 --> 00:25:59,200
Everybody come on over, come to our town!

400
00:26:00,920 --> 00:26:01,920
Start!

